Dashboard Storyboard
MedTrack DV – Hospital Operations & Patient Analytics Dashboard

Module 4 – Dashboard Planning & Prototyping

Prepared By:
Keerthi K M

1. Introduction
Purpose

The Dashboard Storyboard defines the layout, visual components, key performance indicators (KPIs), filters, and navigation flow for the MedTrack DV Tableau dashboards.

The objective is to create an interactive dashboard that helps hospital administrators monitor patient admissions, department performance, resource utilization, and overall hospital operations.

2. Dashboard Architecture
Hospital Overview
        │
        ▼
Patient Flow
        │
        ▼
Department Analytics
        │
        ▼
Resource Utilization

The dashboards are interconnected and share common filters for seamless navigation.

3. Dashboard 1 – Hospital Overview
Objective

Provide an overall summary of hospital performance through key operational metrics.

KPIs
-Total Admissions
-Occupancy Rate
-Average Length of Stay
-Bed Utilization Rate
-Total Revenue
-Department Efficiency Score

Charts
-KPI Cards
-Monthly Admissions Trend (Line Chart)
-Department-wise Admissions (Bar Chart)
-Revenue by Department (Bar Chart)
-Patient Distribution by Diagnosis (Pie Chart)

Filters
-Admission Date
-Department
-Diagnosis
-Gender

5. Dashboard 3 – Department Analytics
Objective

Analyze department performance and doctor workload.

KPIs
-Department Admissions
-Department Efficiency Score
-Average Length of Stay
-Total Revenue by Department

Charts
-Department Admissions (Bar Chart)
-Department Efficiency (Horizontal Bar Chart)
-Revenue by Department
-Doctor-wise Patient Count
-Specialization Distribution

Filters
-Department
-Doctor
-Specialization
-Admission Date

6. Dashboard 4 – Resource Utilization
Objective

Monitor hospital resource utilization and bed allocation.

KPIs
-Occupancy Rate
-Bed Utilization Rate
-Occupied Beds
-Vacant Beds

Charts
-Ward-wise Bed Occupancy
-Bed Type Distribution
-Floor-wise Occupancy
-Occupied vs Vacant Beds
-Surgery Distribution

Filters
-Ward
-Bed Type
-Floor
-Department

7. Global Filters

The following filters will be available across all dashboards.

Admission Date
Department
Doctor
Diagnosis
Gender
Age Group
Ward
Bed Type
Admission Status

8. Dashboard Navigation

Navigation buttons will be provided to switch between the dashboards.

Hospital Overview

↓

Patient Flow

↓

Department Analytics

↓

Resource Utilization

A Home button will be available on each dashboard for quick navigation.

9. Expected Outcome

The dashboard suite will provide:

Hospital performance monitoring
Patient admission analysis
Department performance evaluation
Resource utilization tracking
Financial performance overview
Interactive filtering and navigation

10. Conclusion

This storyboard serves as the design blueprint for the MedTrack DV Tableau dashboards. The proposed layouts, KPIs, visualizations, filters, and navigation ensure a structured and user-friendly dashboard that supports healthcare analytics and operational decision-making.
